<title>JAPAN: MOF to hold 20-year JGB auction on Tuesday.</title>
<headline>MOF to hold 20-year JGB auction on Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Ministry of Finance is planning to offer 20-year Japanese government bonds (JGBs) through a price-competitive auction on Tuesday, a MOF official said on Monday.</p>
<p>A bond market source said the offer volume is likely to be about 400 billion or 500 billion yen and the coupon rate is likely to be set at around 3.3 percent.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-5473-3748</p>
